// LB+datas -- load buffering through data dependencies over racing unordered
// accesses. The paper notes that Wasm non-atomics are weak enough to exhibit
// out-of-thin-air behaviour when racing, and MoRDor's Wasm allows it.
//
// WebAssembly memory model: Watt, Rossberg & Pichon-Pharabod, "Weakening
// WebAssembly" (OOPSLA 2019), Fig. 7. Accesses in mode sc are seqcst, every
// other access unordered.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r1 := x.load(na);
  y.store(r1, na)
} ||| {
  r2 := y.load(na);
  x.store(r2, na)
}
%%
allow (r1 = 42 && r2 = 42) [Wasm]
